====================================================================================
INTERPRETATION
====================================================================================
  If for every k: E[N] consec-MIN (unique) AND C_a (a>=3) consec-MAX (unique),
  AND consec is Pareto-optimal on (-E[N],C_3,C_4,C_5), then EVERY nonneg-weighted
  combination  -alpha*E[N] + sum_{a>=3} w_a C_a  (alpha,w_a >= 0) is consec-max.
  The ONLY obstruction to a clean monotone proof is the LOW corner C_1 (and the
  +C_2 term at k=8): L_y puts weight w_1>0 on C_1 where consec is NOT max. So the
  consec-max of L_y is NOT coordinatewise -- it needs the C_1 deficit to be
  OUTWEIGHED by the (-E[N]) + high-corner surplus.  Quantify that net below.

  --- net-balance audit at k=8 (the binding even-band case) ---
      max-C_1 shape [0, 1, 2, 3, 7, 8, 9, 10]: C_1 surplus over consec = 0.25816
      term ledger (L_y term = weight * functional), shape minus consec:
        d(-E[N]) contribution: -0.494274  (beta=-1)
        w_1=    1 * dC_1=+0.258163  -> +0.258163
        w_2= 1/10 * dC_2=+0.031009  -> +0.003101
        w_3= -1/5 * dC_3=-0.065930  -> +0.013186
        w_4= 1/10 * dC_4=-0.024717  -> -0.002472
        w_5=    1 * dC_5=-0.006122  -> -0.006122
      total L_y(shape)-L_y(consec) = -0.228418  (<0 confirms consec still wins despite C_1 deficit)

DONE.
